  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday Night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1041 AM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nThere are better rain chances on Wednesday as the aforementioned\nupper low retrogrades and pulls additional moistures into Middle\nTennessee, but QPF values are quite modest and we don't anticipate\nanything impactful. By Thursday, temperatures will be at or\nslightly above seasonal norms, and we may see heat indices reach \nthe low 100s in some of the hotter locales. This will remain the \ncase through the weekend, although it appears that we'll stay just\nbelow Heat Advisory criteria each day. Better rain and storm \nchances will spread across all of Middle Tennessee from Friday \nthrough the weekend as the next surface boundary and upper trough \napproach Middle Tennessee from the west, although there's nothing \nyet to hint at much of a severe weather risk. Total QPF from \ntoday through Sunday night continues to represent quite the \ngradient, with values ranging from less than 0.1\" near the \nTennessee River to 1\"+ across portions of the Cumberland Plateau. \nDespite the return of seasonal heat and humidity and persistent \nrain chances, the risk of severe storms, flooding and heat-related\nhazards are all very low throughout the 7-day forecast.",
